{"id": "viva_simulation_core.composites.sepsis_sbml.sepsis_sbml", "name": "sepsis_sbml", "description": "The BioGears sepsis core as its SBML/Antimony extraction (Sauro), run via Tellurium / roadrunner. Emits the 9 shared comparison observables (SBP, DBP, MAP, HR, CO, SVR, blood volume, tissue integrity, blood pathogen). Infection is seeded from `severity` at t = infection_start_s. Healthy at severity 0.", "parameters": {"severity": {"type": "integer", "default": 0, "description": "0 none / 1 mild / 2 moderate / 3 severe (seeds tissue pathogen)"}, "infection_start_s": {"type": "float", "default": 0.0, "description": "Infection start time in seconds (applied only when severity > 0)"}, "interval_s": {"type": "float", "default": 10.0, "description": "Seconds per update"}}, "state": {"tellurium": {"_type": "process", "address": "local:TelluriumProcess", "config": {"model": "", "model_format": "sbml", "model_file": "/Users/eranagmon/code/simulation-core/workspace/investigations/biogears-sbml-sepsis/sources/biogears_sepsis.xml", "integrator": "cvode", "absolute_tolerance": 1e-10, "relative_tolerance": 1e-08, "seed": -1, "species_overrides": {}, "parameter_overrides": {"severity": 0.0}}, "interval": 10.0, "inputs": {}, "outputs": {"species": ["stores", "species"], "rates": ["stores", "rates"], "parameters": ["stores", "parameters"], "time": ["stores", "time"]}, "doc": "Bridge Process wrapping a Tellurium / libroadrunner SBML simulation.\n\nLoads an SBML or Antimony model into a RoadRunner instance and advances\nit in chunks of `interval` on each update() call. Returns absolute\nspecies concentrations, reaction rates, parameter values, and the\ncurrent time as overwrite values.\n\nSPECIES PORT (important):\n  * DEFAULT (``bulk_species=True``): the ``species`` port is a numpy\n    ``array[(n,),float]`` ordered by ``getFloatingSpeciesIds`` and moved via\n    roadrunner's bulk C API \u2014 ~2x faster per update() and bit-identical.\n    Wire it to an Array-shaped store, not a dict.\n  * COUPLED multi-process composites (two+ processes sharing one species\n    store, operator-split): also set ``coupled_species=True`` \u2014 the species\n    output becomes an ADDITIVE array so the arms' deltas SUM under reconcile\n    instead of clobbering, and only the settable subset is written back.\n  * LEGACY (``bulk_species=False``): the old per-species ``map[float]`` port;\n    slower, kept only for back-compat with dict-shaped species stores.\n\nConfig:\n    model: Antimony or SBML source string.\n    model_format: 'antimony' (default) or 'sbml'.\n    model_file: Optional path to a local .ant/.txt/.xml file\n        (takes precedence over `model`).\n    integrator: 'cvode' (deterministic) or 'gillespie' (stochastic).\n    absolute_tolerance: CVODE absolute tolerance.\n    relative_tolerance: CVODE relative tolerance.\n    seed: Random seed for stochastic integrators (None = unset).\n    species_overrides: Mapping of {species_id: initial_value}\n        applied after model load.\n    parameter_overrides: Mapping of {parameter_id: value}\n        applied after model load. These are initial values only: a\n        value on the ``parameters_in`` input port overrides them from\n        the first update() that carries it.\n    reset_on_init: If True, call reset() after applying overrides\n        (default True).", "interval_label": "10 s", "_contract": {"summary": "Advances a user-authored Antimony/SBML kinetic model one coupling interval by integrating its ODE system dX/dt = f(X, p; t) with libroadrunner (CVODE).", "description": "", "inputs": {"species": "optional incoming floating-species state pushed into roadrunner before the step (numpy array ordered by getFloatingSpeciesIds when bulk_species=True, else a {species_id: value} map); in coupled_species mode this is the shared-store baseline the arm starts from", "parameters_in": "{parameter_id: value} global parameter values set in roadrunner before each step; they override parameter_overrides and persist until changed. Ids must be global parameters not defined by an assignment rule; a writer should declare overwrite[...] so its values replace, not add to, the store"}, "outputs": {"species": "post-step floating-species state (overwrite; an ADDITIVE delta in coupled_species mode)", "rates": "{reaction_id: rate} reaction velocities v at the new state (getReactionRates)", "parameters": "{parameter_id: value} global parameter values", "time": "roadrunner current time after the step"}, "config": {"model": "Antimony or SBML source string", "model_format": "'antimony' (default) or 'sbml'", "model_file": "optional path to a local .ant/.txt/.xml model (takes precedence over model)", "integrator": "'cvode' (deterministic, default) or 'gillespie' (stochastic SSA)", "absolute_tolerance": "CVODE absolute tolerance", "relative_tolerance": "CVODE relative tolerance", "seed": "random seed for stochastic integrators (-1 = unset)", "species_overrides": "{species_id: initial_value} applied after model load", "parameter_overrides": "{parameter_id: value} applied after model load (initial values; parameters_in overrides them)", "reset_on_init": "reset() after applying overrides (default True)", "bulk_species": "species port as a numpy Array via roadrunner's bulk C API (default True) vs a legacy map[float]", "coupled_species": "operator-split mode: additive species deltas that SUM under multi-process reconcile", "conserved_moiety_analysis": "let roadrunner slave moiety-dependent species to conservation laws"}, "math": ["\\frac{dX}{dt} = f(X,\\, p;\\, t) = S\\, v(X,\\, p)", "X(t + \\Delta t) = \\mathrm{CVODE}\\big(f,\\, X(t),\\, [t,\\, t + \\Delta t]\\big)", "v = v(X,\\, p) \\quad\\text{(reaction-rate vector returned on the } \\texttt{rates} \\text{ port)}", "\\text{coupled mode: } X_{n+1} = X_n + \\textstyle\\sum_i \\big(X^{(i)} - X_n\\big)"], "symbols": {"X": "floating-species state vector (concentrations by default, or amounts), ordered by getFloatingSpeciesIds", "p": "global kinetic parameters of the model", "t": "simulation time", "\\Delta t": "coupling interval advanced per update() call", "f": "ODE right-hand side assembled by libroadrunner from the model's reactions", "S": "stoichiometry matrix", "v": "reaction-rate (flux) vector", "X^{(i)}": "the i-th coupled arm's post-step state in operator-split (coupled_species) mode"}, "assumptions": ["Deterministic CVODE (BDF) integration by default; stiffness is handled internally by CVODE. Set integrator='gillespie' for stochastic SSA.", "The reaction network is user-authored (Antimony/SBML) and loaded at build time, so this contract specifies the integration and port semantics, not any specific reaction equations.", "Species are reported as concentrations unless the model yields amounts; the state vector is ordered by getFloatingSpeciesIds.", "update() is stateful across intervals (roadrunner carries state between calls); the Step variants reset each firing instead.", "coupled_species assumes a Lie/Jacobi operator split across processes sharing one species store; each arm emits its own delta and the deltas sum under reconcile."], "references": ["Somogyi et al. (2015) libRoadRunner: a high performance SBML simulation and analysis library.", "Hindmarsh et al. (2005) SUNDIALS: CVODE stiff/non-stiff ODE integration."], "face": {"inputs": {}, "outputs": {}}, "amendments": []}, "_inputs": {"species": "maybe[array[(0),float]]", "model_in": "maybe[string]", "parameters_in": "map[float]"}, "_outputs": {"species": "overwrite[array[(0),float]]", "rates": "overwrite[map[float]]", "parameters": "overwrite[map[float]]", "time": "overwrite[float]"}}, "stores": {"species": "[]", "parameters": {"BV": 5517.73, "SBP0": 114.0, "DBP0": 73.5, "HR0": 72.0, "CO0": 97.2, "HRmax": 177.2, "HRmin": 0.001, "srm": 0.849, "lacm": 0.4333, "sR": 0.8803103459, "sC": 1.0, "sRao": 1.0, "sCao": 1.166785426, "sRrh": 1.0, "sCvc": 1.019216356, "P_VC0": 3.7962, "P_LV0": 121.6, "P_RH0": 19.0004, "R_ra": 5.94e-05, "R_la": 8.9e-05, "R_RP